mcp__codex_apps__slack_slack_read_channel
Reads messages from a Slack channel in reverse chronological order (newest first). To read DM history, use a user_id as channel_id. Read-only.

Use slack_read_thread with message_ts to read thread replies. Use slack_search_channels to find a channel ID by name. Use slack_search_public to search across channels. If 'channel_not_found', try slack_search_channels first. This tool is part of plugin `Slack`.

Share work and pull context

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__codex_apps__slack_slack_read_channel(args: {
  // ID of the Channel, private group, or IM channel to fetch history for. Can also be a user_id to read DM history.
  channel_id: string;
  // Paginate through collections of data by setting the cursor parameter to a next_cursor attribute returned by a previous request
  cursor?: string;
  // End of time range of messages to include in results (timestamp)
  latest?: string;
  // Number of messages to return, between 1 and 100. Default value is 100.
  limit?: number;
  // Start of time range of messages to include in results (timestamp)
  oldest?: string;
  // Level of detail: 'detailed' (default, includes reactions + thread info) or 'concise'.
  response_format?: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

mcp__codex_apps__slack_slack_search_channels
Search for Slack channels by name or description. Returns channel names, IDs, topics, purposes, and archive status.

Keyword tips: use terms matching channel names/descriptions (e.g., "engineering", "\"project alpha\""). Names are typically lowercase with hyphens.

Use slack_read_channel to read messages from a known channel. Use slack_search_public to search message content across channels.
---
Split your search query into 2 fields:

1. `keywords` — Lexical terms that must appear in the channel's name or attributes. Each element should be a single word or "quoted phrase". All AND'd.

2. `natural_language_query` — User's question in conversational tone for semantic re-ranking. Preserve original phrasing; on follow-ups incorporate prior context.

Require `natural_language_query` + `keywords`.

❌ Semantic search is not available for this user.

Strategy: Use keywords for subject terms. If 0 results, broaden by simplifying keywords.
---. This tool is part of plugin `Slack`.

Share work and pull context

exec tool declaration:
